DAY_DATA = {'day': 154, 'part1_intro': "Day 154 — Altostrat Media — content and AI requirements — uses the roadmap's case or exam scope as the input. Each topic names the decision boundary, evidence owner and business effect; no product choice or score is treated as a fact without supporting evidence.", 'part2_intro': 'Trace the full reasoning path: supplied fact or requirement, candidate design or study rule, acceptance evidence, failure signal, owner and condition that would change the choice. The topology is a teaching model, not evidence of a live system or exam result.', 'part3_intro': 'These deep-dive cases preserve the original case or exam reasoning while separating supplied facts from architectural inference. The incident diagrams are synthetic exercises, not observed production events.', 'part4_intro': "The labs retain each day's original decision work, expanded into the eight execution stages used on Day 142. Complete them with prior artifacts and synthetic inputs unless an earlier roadmap page explicitly authorizes a cloud test.", 'exit_summary': 'A source-linked requirements matrix and an existing-versus-proposed system/data-flow diagram with owners, evidence types and open questions.', 'arch_table_html': '\n<table><caption>Day-specific architecture and evidence path</caption><thead><tr><th>Topic boundary</th><th>Decision rule</th><th>Acceptance evidence</th><th>Limit</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td>Read the official case and extract requirements</td><td>Separate supplied fact, requirement and proposed control.</td><td>One artifact, one rejected alternative and one changed-constraint result.</td><td>Local/tabletop evidence cannot prove production behavior or exam performance.</td></tr><tr><td>Separate content AI capabilities from control and operating requirements</td><td>Separate supplied fact, requirement and proposed control.</td><td>One artifact, one rejected alternative and one changed-constraint result.</td><td>Local/tabletop evidence cannot prove production behavior or exam performance.</td></tr></tbody></table>', 'arch_diagram': {'type': 'topology', 'title': 'Day 154: Altostrat Media — content and AI requirements — evidence and decision path', 'desc': 'Three-tier architecture path for Altostrat Media — content and AI requirements, showing case or exam inputs, requirements and trade-off evidence, then acceptance and ownership controls.', 'caption': 'Scope: a synthetic evidence path for Day 154 covering Read the official case and extract require / Separate content AI capabilities from cont. It shows reasoning boundaries and verification ownership; it does not prove a production deployment, exam result, price, quota, eligibility or customer outcome.', 'width': 1120, 'height': 690, 'layers': [{'name': 'TIER 1 · INPUTS / DEMAND', 'desc': 'case facts, prompts and constraints', 'x': 10, 'y': 55, 'w': 1100, 'h': 92, 'fill': '#0c2033', 'title_color': '#38bdf8', 'opacity': 0.72}, {'name': 'TIER 2 · EVIDENCE / REASONING', 'desc': 'requirements, alternatives and failure checks', 'x': 10, 'y': 185, 'w': 1100, 'h': 210, 'fill': '#241808', 'title_color': '#f59e0b', 'opacity': 0.64}, {'name': 'TIER 3 · GOVERNANCE / ACCEPTANCE', 'desc': 'owners, acceptance and revisit triggers', 'x': 10, 'y': 435, 'w': 1100, 'h': 115, 'fill': '#062316', 'title_color': '#22c55e', 'opacity': 0.68}], 'components': [{'name': 'Case or prompt', 'detail': 'Day 154 supplied scope', 'x': 60, 'y': 78, 'w': 250, 'h': 56, 'stroke': '#38bdf8', 'fill': '#102a42'}, {'name': 'Prior artifacts', 'detail': 'facts + decisions + errors', 'x': 435, 'y': 78, 'w': 250, 'h': 56, 'stroke': '#38bdf8', 'fill': '#102a42'}, {'name': 'Changed constraint', 'detail': 'cost / risk / scope', 'x': 810, 'y': 78, 'w': 250, 'h': 56, 'stroke': '#38bdf8', 'fill': '#102a42'}, {'name': 'Requirements map', 'detail': 'fact to acceptance', 'x': 60, 'y': 220, 'w': 250, 'h': 105, 'stroke': '#f59e0b', 'fill': '#3b2508'}, {'name': 'Option matrix', 'detail': 'choice + alternative', 'x': 435, 'y': 220, 'w': 250, 'h': 105, 'stroke': '#f59e0b', 'fill': '#3b2508'}, {'name': 'Failure rehearsal', 'detail': 'signal + safe response', 'x': 810, 'y': 220, 'w': 250, 'h': 105, 'stroke': '#f59e0b', 'fill': '#3b2508'}, {'name': 'Evidence owner', 'detail': 'source + artifact', 'x': 245, 'y': 455, 'w': 250, 'h': 70, 'stroke': '#22c55e', 'fill': '#064e3b'}, {'name': 'Acceptance gate', 'detail': 'observed / predicted', 'x': 625, 'y': 455, 'w': 250, 'h': 70, 'stroke': '#22c55e', 'fill': '#064e3b'}], 'flows': [{'x1': 185, 'y1': 134, 'x2': 185, 'y2': 220, 'type': 'ok', 'label': 'extract'}, {'x1': 560, 'y1': 134, 'x2': 560, 'y2': 220, 'type': 'ok', 'label': 'trace'}, {'x1': 935, 'y1': 134, 'x2': 935, 'y2': 220, 'type': 'warn', 'label': 'challenge'}, {'x1': 310, 'y1': 272, 'x2': 435, 'y2': 272, 'type': 'ok', 'label': 'compare'}, {'x1': 685, 'y1': 272, 'x2': 810, 'y2': 272, 'type': 'ok', 'label': 'rehearse'}, {'x1': 935, 'y1': 325, 'x2': 750, 'y2': 455, 'type': 'ok', 'label': 'accept'}, {'x1': 560, 'y1': 325, 'x2': 370, 'y2': 455, 'type': 'warn', 'label': 'evidence'}, {'x1': 495, 'y1': 490, 'x2': 625, 'y2': 490, 'type': 'ok', 'label': 'review'}], 'boundaries': [{'x': 42, 'y': 205, 'w': 1036, 'h': 140, 'color': '#f59e0b', 'label': 'EVIDENCE CHECK'}, {'x': 220, 'y': 442, 'w': 680, 'h': 94, 'color': '#22c55e', 'label': 'DECISION OWNER'}], 'probes': [{'cx': 185, 'cy': 106, 'label': 'PROBE 1 · input classified', 'badge': 'P1', 'color': '#38bdf8'}, {'cx': 560, 'cy': 272, 'label': 'PROBE 2 · trade-off recorded', 'badge': 'P2', 'color': '#f59e0b'}, {'cx': 750, 'cy': 490, 'label': 'PROBE 3 · acceptance result', 'badge': 'P3', 'color': '#22c55e'}]}, 'topics': [{'key': 'topic-01', 'title': 'Read the official case and extract requirements', 'overview': 'Altostrat’s case describes an established media platform, a modernization direction and a set of business and technical requirements. First capture what already exists: GKE, Cloud Storage, BigQuery, Cloud Run functions, on-premises ingestion/archive, mixed identity providers and mixed monitoring. Then capture what the business wants to improve.', 'preview': 'Symptom: A media asset is ingested on premises, copied to Cloud Storage, processed for metadata and summarized, then surfaced in search and recommendations. Effect: The read the official case and extract requirements decision remains unverified.', 'technical': '\n<p>The official case states that Altostrat has a GKE-based content management and delivery platform; media documents, audio and video are in Cloud Storage; BigQuery is the primary warehouse; Cloud Run functions perform event-driven work such as transcoding, metadata extraction and personalized recommendations. It also states that some ingestion and archival workflows remain on premises, identity uses Google Identity and third-party providers, and observability combines Cloud Monitoring and Prometheus with email alerts.</p>\n<table><caption>Supplied facts versus design work</caption><thead><tr><th>Case statement</th><th>Requirement implied by the case</th><th>Design question</th><th>Evidence needed</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td>GKE delivers the platform</td><td>Containerized workloads must be deployable and operable across the relevant environments.</td><td>Which workloads truly need Kubernetes, and what must remain compatible on premises?</td><td>Workload inventory, dependency map, deployment and failure tests.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Cloud Storage holds diverse media</td><td>Storage must scale while controlling lifecycle and retrieval cost.</td><td>Which assets need hot access, retention, versioning, restore or legal hold?</td><td>Object-size/access distribution, retention policy, restore acceptance and current pricing check.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>BigQuery analyzes behavior and demographics</td><td>Analytics must inform content strategy and decisions.</td><td>What events are collected, at what grain, and which data is sensitive?</td><td>Event contract, lineage, access matrix, freshness target and query-cost baseline.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>On-premises ingestion/archive remains</td><td>Hybrid data movement must be secure, observable and recoverable.</td><td>Which side owns the source of truth during migration or replay?</td><td>Connectivity path, DNS/routing ownership, transfer reconciliation and rollback plan.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>AI must be auditable and explainable</td><td>Generated results need provenance, evaluation and a decision record.</td><td>What is published automatically, what requires review, and how is a decision appealed?</td><td>Prompt/model/version metadata, source references, evaluation set, reviewer outcome and retention rule.</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>The right first diagram has separate paths for source media, derived media, metadata, user events, AI requests and editorial publication. Draw control boundaries around identity, ingestion, processing, model access, review and delivery. A single “AI service” box obscures whether a request is synchronous, queued, replayable, human-approved or allowed to publish.</p>\n<div class="further"><h4>Further study</h4><p><a href="../sources.html#topic-047">Topic 047 source section</a> links to the <a href="https://services.google.com/fh/files/misc/v6.1_pca_altostrat_media_case_study_english.pdf" rel="noopener noreferrer">official Altostrat Media case PDF</a>. The case’s supplied facts are the baseline; current product behavior and limits still require current documentation and testing.</p></div>\n<p><a href="../sources.html#topic-047">Topic 047 source section</a>; current publisher material was checked 2026-09-30. Separate supplied facts, local observations and proposed controls.</p>', 'questions': ['Which supplied fact, requirement or artifact controls the choice?', 'Which credible alternative is rejected, and what evidence would make it preferable?', 'Which failure signal reveals the first broken boundary?', 'What is observed, supplied, predicted or still unknown?'], 'reference': 'https://services.google.com/fh/files/misc/v6.1_pca_altostrat_media_case_study_english.pdf', 'reference_label': 'Official Topic 47 source (checked 2026-09-30)', 'scenario': {'scenario': 'A media asset is ingested on premises, copied to Cloud Storage, processed for metadata and summarized, then surfaced in search and recommendations. The proposal does not identify the authoritative asset ID or whether derived results can be replayed. A retry can create duplicate catalog entries, while a partial transfer can make analytics disagree with the editorial system.', 'impact': '', 'constraints': 'Maintain content availability, protect the hybrid boundary, preserve lineage and avoid treating a successful transfer command as proof of reconciliation.', 'facts': 'The case statement and artifact are teaching inputs; no production incident or learner result is claimed.', 'inference': 'Assign a stable asset ID and version, record source and derived-object checksums, make processing idempotent, and separate transfer acknowledgement from business acceptance. Define the source of truth for each state, a replay window, a dead-letter path and a reconciliation report. Measure freshness, completeness and failed/replayed work.', 'root': 'Assign a stable asset ID and version, record source and derived-object checksums, make processing idempotent, and separate transfer acknowledgement from business acceptance. Define the source of truth for each state, a replay window, a dead-letter path and a reconciliation report. Measure freshness, completeness and failed/replayed work.', 'fix': 'Assign a stable asset ID and version, record source and derived-object checksums, make processing idempotent, and separate transfer acknowledgement from business acceptance. Define the source of truth for each state, a replay window, a dead-letter path and a reconciliation report. Measure freshness, completeness and failed/replayed work.', 'verify': 'Re-run the bounded case, compare it with the declared acceptance signal and save the resulting decision trace.', 'residual': 'Storage lifecycle and transfer cost, source metadata quality and on-premises failure behavior still require the owner’s data and a current design review.', 'diagram': ('supplied trigger', 'missing or untested control', 'business and operating impact', 'bounded defensive control', 'verified evidence artifact')}, 'lab': {'name': 'Read the official case and extract requirements', 'goal': 'Build a source-linked fact and requirement register for Altostrat without turning proposed services into case facts.', 'expected': 'Expected state A fact register and system/data-flow diagram that another architect can trace back to the official case, with proposed design choices visibly separated.', 'mode': 'local/tabletop with synthetic data; no cloud access or spend.', 'prereq': 'the official case PDF and Day 153 decision-defense habits.', 'preflight': 'Use `day-154-altostrat-requirements.md` and record the source, access date, prior artifact, owner and synthetic-data boundary.', 'steps': ['**Stage 1 — Preflight and validate assumptions/environment.** Create `day-154-altostrat-requirements.md`. Record Day 154, the prior artifact, the source `https://services.google.com/fh/files/misc/v6.1_pca_altostrat_media_case_study_english.pdf`, the access date, a named owner and the statement that the exercise uses synthetic or tabletop evidence only.', '**Stage 2 — Prepare the target, inputs, or backing resources.** Preflight. Create day-154-altostrat-requirements.md . Record the source URL, date, lab mode and synthetic-data boundary.', '**Stage 3 — Author the plan, configuration, or analysis.** Extract. Create statement | page | fact or requirement | owner | evidence needed columns. Capture the existing GKE, Cloud Storage, BigQuery, Cloud Run functions, on-premises, identity and observability statements.', '**Stage 4 — Execute or simulate the planned change.** Classify. Split business requirements from technical requirements. Add success measures for availability, cost, freshness, quality, safety, support and auditability without inventing target values.', '**Stage 5 — Inspect expected state and verify outcomes.** Map boundaries. Draw source media, derived media, metadata, analytics, AI, review, identity and delivery paths. Mark what is existing, proposed, unknown and retired.', '**Stage 6 — Rehearse a bounded failure, edge case, or decision challenge.** Inject a change. Remove hybrid connectivity, double storage volume, or require an editorial review gate. Record the first affected boundary, changed signal and a credible alternative.', '**Stage 7 — Diagnose evidence and record remediation/decision.** Close out. Save the matrix and link it from the daily artifact. List the questions that need owner confirmation, current product documentation or a bounded test.', '**Stage 8 — Clean up or close out the exercise.** Save `day-154-altostrat-requirements.md`, link it from the daily artifact, keep the evidence, remove only disposable copies and state what needs an authorized or production verification.'], 'verification': 'Expected state A fact register and system/data-flow diagram that another architect can trace back to the official case, with proposed design choices visibly separated.', 'accept': 'Expected state A fact register and system/data-flow diagram that another architect can trace back to the official case, with proposed design choices visibly separated.', 'trouble': 'Troubleshooting If a statement names a technology but not its role, record the role as an inference. If a requirement has no measurable signal, write the question instead of manufacturing a target.', 'cleanup': 'Keep the evidence artifact and remove only disposable copies. No cloud resource, credential, payment detail or protected exam content belongs in this exercise.', 'file': 'day-154-altostrat-requirements.md'}}, {'key': 'topic-02', 'title': 'Separate content AI capabilities from control and operating requirements', 'overview': 'Summarization, metadata extraction, harmful-content detection, trend analysis, recommendations and conversational support are capabilities. Auditability, human or editorial review, identity, data lineage, cost controls, hybrid connectivity, deployment, monitoring and rollback are operating requirements around those capabilities.', 'preview': 'Symptom: An automatically generated summary and harmful-content label are sent directly to the user experience. Effect: The separate content ai capabilities from control and operating requirements decision remains unverified.', 'technical': '\n<p>A useful Altostrat design treats AI output as a derived, reviewable artifact rather than an unquestioned replacement for the source media. A typical flow is: ingest and identify the asset; extract audio, video and technical metadata; transcribe or analyze with the selected model; produce a summary, tags or moderation result; attach provenance and confidence; route uncertain or harmful results to review; publish only after the acceptance rule passes; and emit immutable audit evidence.</p>\n<table><caption>AI requirement to control mapping</caption><thead><tr><th>Capability</th><th>Control boundary</th><th>Failure to rehearse</th><th>Acceptance signal</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td>Summarization</td><td>Source asset, transcript/version, model/prompt version, reviewer state</td><td>Summary invents a claim or omits a material qualification.</td><td>Evaluation set meets the declared quality threshold and every output links to source/provenance.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Metadata enrichment</td><td>Schema, confidence, taxonomy owner and update policy</td><td>Incorrect tags make search or recommendations misleading.</td><td>Field-level validation, sampled precision/recall review and rollback of a bad model version.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Harmful-content detection</td><td>Policy, model result, escalation queue and publication gate</td><td>Unsafe content is published, or legitimate content is silently blocked.</td><td>Known test set, threshold review, appeal path and audit trail for each decision.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Recommendations and conversational support</td><td>User identity, consent, retrieval corpus, tool permissions and response logging</td><td>Private data leaks or the assistant takes an unauthorized action.</td><td>Access tests, grounding/citation checks, refusal tests and bounded tool calls.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Trend analysis</td><td>Event definitions, aggregation window, demographic access and retention</td><td>Incomplete or biased events drive a false content decision.</td><td>Freshness, completeness, lineage and decision-owner review.</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Separate the online path from the batch path. A user-facing assistant may need bounded latency and a safe degraded response; a large media summarization job can be queued, retried and throttled. Both paths need idempotency, dead-letter handling, model/version traceability, cost attribution and a rollback or reprocessing plan. Do not infer that GKE, Cloud Run functions, BigQuery or Cloud Storage automatically supplies these controls.</p>\n<div class="callout"><strong>Design rule</strong><p>Every AI result must answer four questions: which source and version produced it, which model and configuration produced it, who or what approved its use, and what happens when it is wrong. If one answer is missing, the result is a draft, not a publication-grade decision.</p></div>\n<p><a href="../sources.html#topic-047">Topic 047 source section</a>; current publisher material was checked 2026-09-30. Separate supplied facts, local observations and proposed controls.</p>', 'questions': ['Which supplied fact, requirement or artifact controls the choice?', 'Which credible alternative is rejected, and what evidence would make it preferable?', 'Which failure signal reveals the first broken boundary?', 'What is observed, supplied, predicted or still unknown?'], 'reference': 'https://services.google.com/fh/files/misc/v6.1_pca_altostrat_media_case_study_english.pdf', 'reference_label': 'Official Topic 47 source (checked 2026-09-30)', 'scenario': {'scenario': 'An automatically generated summary and harmful-content label are sent directly to the user experience. Reviewers cannot identify the source segment, model version or threshold that produced a decision. A false negative can expose harmful content; a false positive can suppress legitimate journalism; a hallucinated summary can damage trust.', 'impact': '', 'constraints': 'Support diverse media, keep the service available, give users a useful fallback and retain enough evidence for an appeal or incident review.', 'facts': 'The case statement and artifact are teaching inputs; no production incident or learner result is claimed.', 'inference': 'Make AI results versioned drafts with provenance, confidence and policy state. Add an evaluation set, threshold ownership, human review for defined classes, refusal/degraded responses, immutable decision logs and a rollback path. Limit assistants to authorized retrieval and tools; do not grant publication authority merely because a model returned a high score.', 'root': 'Make AI results versioned drafts with provenance, confidence and policy state. Add an evaluation set, threshold ownership, human review for defined classes, refusal/degraded responses, immutable decision logs and a rollback path. Limit assistants to authorized retrieval and tools; do not grant publication authority merely because a model returned a high score.', 'fix': 'Make AI results versioned drafts with provenance, confidence and policy state. Add an evaluation set, threshold ownership, human review for defined classes, refusal/degraded responses, immutable decision logs and a rollback path. Limit assistants to authorized retrieval and tools; do not grant publication authority merely because a model returned a high score.', 'verify': 'Run a synthetic test set containing benign, ambiguous and disallowed examples. Record quality by class, review time, false positives/negatives and the exact model/configuration. The result is a bounded evaluation, not proof of production safety across all languages or content types.', 'residual': 'Run a synthetic test set containing benign, ambiguous and disallowed examples. Record quality by class, review time, false positives/negatives and the exact model/configuration. The result is a bounded evaluation, not proof of production safety across all languages or content types.', 'diagram': ('supplied trigger', 'missing or untested control', 'business and operating impact', 'bounded defensive control', 'verified evidence artifact')}, 'lab': {'name': 'Separate content AI capabilities from control and operating requirements', 'goal': 'Turn one Altostrat capability into a bounded, auditable AI workflow with a safe failure mode.', 'expected': 'Expected state A bounded AI decision path with provenance, versioning, access control, evaluation, human or policy gate, failure behavior and residual-risk owner.', 'mode': 'local/tabletop with synthetic media metadata; no model endpoint or cloud spend.', 'prereq': 'the Day 154 requirements matrix.', 'preflight': 'Use `day-154-ai-content-decision.md` and record the source, access date, prior artifact, owner and synthetic-data boundary.', 'steps': ['**Stage 1 — Preflight and validate assumptions/environment.** Create `day-154-ai-content-decision.md`. Record Day 154, the prior artifact, the source `https://services.google.com/fh/files/misc/v6.1_pca_altostrat_media_case_study_english.pdf`, the access date, a named owner and the statement that the exercise uses synthetic or tabletop evidence only.', '**Stage 2 — Prepare the target, inputs, or backing resources.** Choose one path. Use synthetic input for summarization, metadata enrichment, harmful-content detection, recommendation or conversational support. Record why the path matters to the case.', '**Stage 3 — Author the plan, configuration, or analysis.** Define the contract. Write asset_id | source version | input fields | model/config version | output schema | confidence | reviewer state | retention | owner .', '**Stage 4 — Execute or simulate the planned change.** Define controls. State the authorization boundary, provenance link, evaluation set, human-review rule, refusal/degraded response, rollback trigger and cost/freshness signal.', '**Stage 5 — Inspect expected state and verify outcomes.** Inject failure. Use a missing transcript, low confidence, unsafe label, stale source or unauthorized retrieval request. Record the first changed signal and the safe outcome.', '**Stage 6 — Rehearse a bounded failure, edge case, or decision challenge.** Accept or reject. Mark the output draft, reviewable or publishable according to the declared rule. Record one rejected alternative and the condition under which it could become acceptable.', '**Stage 7 — Diagnose evidence and record remediation/decision.** Close out. Save day-154-ai-content-decision.md , link it from the daily artifact and state what still requires an evaluation set, security review, data-owner approval or production test.', '**Stage 8 — Clean up or close out the exercise.** Save `day-154-ai-content-decision.md`, link it from the daily artifact, keep the evidence, remove only disposable copies and state what needs an authorized or production verification.'], 'verification': 'Expected state A bounded AI decision path with provenance, versioning, access control, evaluation, human or policy gate, failure behavior and residual-risk owner.', 'accept': 'Expected state A bounded AI decision path with provenance, versioning, access control, evaluation, human or policy gate, failure behavior and residual-risk owner.', 'trouble': 'Troubleshooting A high confidence score is not an explanation. If the source, model/configuration or reviewer state is missing, keep the output in draft status.', 'cleanup': 'Keep the evidence artifact and remove only disposable copies. No cloud resource, credential, payment detail or protected exam content belongs in this exercise.', 'file': 'day-154-ai-content-decision.md'}}]}
